    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_identity",
      "statement": "Correct objects, chemical bookkeeping and valid evidence.",
      "expected": "Inspect species_registry, every input/geometry mapping and real raw log. Verify stoichiometry, charge/multiplicity, method/state, stationarity or constrained label, and consistent thermochemistry. Use the full neutral singlet INT-G C39H34OP2Pd reactant. In its fixed map, Pd75 binds hydrides H76/H77 and P1/P41 of XantPhos. Build the H–H saddle, eta2-H2 adduct, separated H2+Pd(XantPhos), and one DMAc-coordinated Pd regeneration endpoint. Keep the XantPhos graph intact. Use DMAc and 298.15 K. Primary ledger: solutes 1 M and H2 at 1 atm; separately report all-species 1 M and H2 pressure sensitivity. Source 1 atm and all-solute 1 M values cannot be combined.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "source_1",
        "source_2",
        "upgrade_design"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_HH_formation",
      "statement": "Connected H–H formation saddle and bound-H2 endpoint.",
      "expected": "Connected H–H formation saddle and bound-H2 endpoint. Recompute quantities from identified raw jobs and evidence files. Check all required named matrix cells; prose or a legacy scalar cannot replace this endpoint. A scientific ambiguity is valid only after the relevant controls exist. Non-saddle/collapse alternatives require actual profiles and both endpoints, not failed optimization. A same-basin comparison may omit nonexistent independent numeric operands only after separate complete searches, mapped identity and stationarity demonstrate collapse; this never excuses a missing control. New numerical reference and tolerances are pending; never choose a preferred value or broaden a legacy tolerance to excuse wrong identity.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "source_1",
        "source_2",
        "upgrade_design"
      ]
    },
